s=open('pieces.py').read()
a=s.index('"""+R(188,215)+"""')
NEW='''"""+"""
S3 Design [condensed; clauses kept]
C3.1 Orbits/folds inherited: A{0,5,10,15}, B{1,4,11,14}, C{2,7,8,13}, D{3,6,9,12}; six directed 2+2 folds AB->CD, CD->AB, AC->BD, BD->AC, AD->BC, BC->AD. Representative = smallest prefix (A0, B1, C2, D3). Flip masks: 5 = flip-X (mu_x->-mu_x, kappa->-kappa), 10 = flip-Y, 15 = flip-XY (kappa unchanged). Class label g(a) = a XOR rep(orbit(a)) in {I, X, Y, XY}: I = 0,1,2,3; X = 5,4,7,6; Y = 10,11,8,9; XY = 15,14,13,12 (orbits A,B,C,D). All reps have mu_x > 0, mu_y > 0, so here the group-element class coincides with the sign quadrant (CNA's (s_x,s_y) partition); E37-5's definition governs if they ever differ. chi(g) = s_x*s_y (I +1, X -1, Y -1, XY +1); kappa_a = chi(g(a))*kappa_rep. Kappa has no single sign within a class (class I: +0.1114, -0.0120, -0.1951, +0.0171). Each fold has 2 fitting and 2 evaluation prefixes per class: identifiable, not evidence of sufficient support.
C3.2 Class model: per system S, fold f, class g: full 3x8 B_{f,g} on the class-g fitting prefixes; fixed-kappa B_mu,{f,g} with kappa row 0 and mu rows on the reduced 2-column design (E36-3). Objective: E36-3 weighted LS on ALL output components, w(a,u) = P_h(a,u), all 16 continuations: min sum_{a in fit(f), class g} sum_u w ||L_a(u) X - J_a(u)||^2, J_a = S's local response map, L_a = dPhi/dtheta at S's own baseline chart. Same maps for ALL, MARG, XOR. A class map is applied unchanged to class-g prefixes of the evaluation orbits.
C3.3 Solver/rank inherited: one SVD of the sqrt(w)-weighted design; sigma_i/sigma_1 > 1e-6 resolved, < 1e-10 zero, [1e-10,1e-6] UNRESOLVED (E36-8); min-norm, rcond 1e-10; B2: resolved lower rank is fitted min-norm and SCORED (rank, sigma_1 reported); only UNRESOLVED cells go unscored and stay in the denominator; applied to every (system, fold, class) and global design.
C3.4 Global B and B_mu per fold fitted for every system with the same solver: a fixed descriptive comparator (#37 L116); no global statistic decides an outcome except the C4 identities.
C3.5 Freeze-before-scoring: compute all global and class fits from fitting prefixes only, write with stored terms to outputs/fit_freeze_<system>.json and fsync, only then propagate evaluation edits; no refit after evaluation begins.
C3.6 Stored outputs (E37-8), float64 little-endian with raw-byte sha256: (a) every fitted B and B_mu, global and per class, every system and fold, in full (plus augmented maps under Option B); (b) full sigma list, sigma_1, ratios, rank, unresolved flag, n_inverted per design; (c) L_mu, L_full, S, measured gain per (system, fit type, fold, class, eval orbit, group, eps), weighted and unweighted, with scoreable counts and law mass; (d) per-prefix G_a (3x3) and r_a (3x8), per (fold, class) and per fold sums, mu-mu block and mu rows of sum r; (e) cancellation diagnostics: per (system, orbit) sums of G_a[kappa,mu_x], G_a[kappa,mu_y], G_a[mu_x,mu_y]; for two-coordinate systems sum G_a[kk]*Dg(mu_a); per (prefix, flip) max|G_{g.a} - R_g G_a R_g| with R_X = diag(-1,1,-1), R_Y = diag(1,-1,-1), R_XY = diag(-1,-1,1). Descriptive identity checks only.
C3.7 Disclosure: the class label is supplied by the analyst; each class model has 4x the parameters (4x24 full, 4x16 fixed-kappa, vs 24 and 16); success would not show any network contains or consults the label; four class maps address only the declared flip-class form of variation.
C3.8 Diagnostics only: kappa-row norms (scale depends on fitted coordinates); optional per-prefix local fits (use evaluation Jacobians, abandon the held-out claim). Neither enters any outcome.
C3.9 Voiding: SYS-NC1-NC3 (baseline chart not the true chart) inherit N4(ii) per-prefix voiding and the >= 5-of-16 RESTRICTED COMPARATOR NOT ADMISSIBLE ceiling. A class with 0 non-voided fitting prefixes in a fold is a rank-UNRESOLVED cell. Proposed rule (B1 extended): if any (fold, class) design of a system is UNRESOLVED, that system's pooled class statistic is not formed (REFERENCE RANK UNRESOLVED). Void-and-pool withdrawn by CNA (Q3).
C3.10 Pooling (E36-5): occurrences pooled with original w(a,u), equal direction/sign weights, normalized once over pooled scoreable occurrences; fold-normalized losses never averaged; class statistic pools 6 folds x 4 classes; H, S and ratio share masks and weights.

S4 Systems and derived expectations [condensed; clauses kept]
Notation: theta = (mu_x, mu_y, kappa), forecast Phi; q_X = m_x, q_Y = m_y, q_XOR = m_x + m_y - 2(m_x m_y + c). Under flip-X outputs map (q_X,q_Y,q_XOR) -> (1-q_X, q_Y, 1-q_XOR), so dPhi changes by P_X = diag(-1,1,-1) (P_Y analogous). Premise P0: with the O1 terminal-flip and probability-invariance fixtures, L_{g.a}(g.u) = P_g L_a(u) R_g, w(g.a,g.u) = w(a,u), hence G_{g.a} = R_g G_a R_g. UNVERIFIED numerically.
C4.0 P0 step-0 fixture: after O1 and O2, before any fit of any system. On the true-chart closed-form L_a(u) (shared by SYS-O6, SYS-PC, SYS-LIM), for every prefix, flip g in {X,Y,XY} and continuation u: (i) max|L_{g.a}(g.u) - P_g L_a(u) R_g| <= tol_P0; (ii) w(g.a,g.u) = w(a,u) exactly; (iii) max|G_{g.a} - R_g G_a R_g| <= tol_P0 (g.u by masks 85/170 on full histories). Also run and reported on the SYS-FK product chart and SYS-NC1 chart (flip-symmetric); not on NC2/NC3 (symmetry broken by design). tol_P0 TO BE FIXED BEFORE FREEZE. A P0 failure on true-chart designs = PIPELINE INVALID (DERIVATION PREMISE), stop before any fit, no rerun. After P0 passes, a D1, D2 or D4 failure on a resolved design = PIPELINE INVALID (IMPLEMENTATION), also stop (Q5). SYS-O6, SYS-PC, SYS-FK are implementation/positive controls with expected identities; SYS-NC1-NC3 are confound controls (E37-7), gain reported, not passed or failed.
C4.1 SYS-O6 (O6 exactly: state, readout, Q seed 35006, edits; keeps its positive implementation role, #37 L124). Expected: global B = D Q^T to <= 1e-9 and Pred_full error <= 1e-9 on every scoreable edit; every class B_{f,g} = D Q^T to <= 1e-9 whenever resolved rank 3. B_mu,{f,g} = C_mu + (sum G_mumu)^-1 (sum G_mukappa) c_kappa over the class's two fitting prefixes, generally != 0 (cross term cancels only over whole orbits), so the class comparator loss may differ from O6's global value (UNVERIFIED). A new package containing the O6 system as a control, not a rerun (Q13).
C4.2 SYS-PC "PC+-" (E37-6; #37 L125; CNA's PC+ made concrete).
- (a) State psi = (mu_x, mu_y, tau), tau = sign(mu_x mu_y)*kappa; by C3.1 tau_a = kappa_rep(orbit(a)), flip-invariant, constant within an orbit. z = Q D_psi^-1 (psi - psi_bar), Q the 8x3 seed-35006 matrix (reuse TO BE FIXED BEFORE FREEZE); psi_bar, D_psi P-weighted mean/SD over the 16 prefixes computed in-package.
- (b) Readout (autonomous): psi = D_psi Q^T z + psi_bar; theta = (psi1, psi2, sign(psi1 psi2)*psi3); forecast with Phi. Class/sign information is carried by the state and used by the readout; the analyst label never generates responses. Baseline chart = true theta_a (sign^2 = 1), so L_a, weights and global/class designs are identical to O6's; global designs known resolved; class design ranks UNVERIFIED.
- (c) Local map: C = D_psi Q^T (rows c_x, c_y, c_tau), S_a = diag(1,1,chi_a), J_a(u) = L_a(u) S_a C, exact for non-crossing finite edits.
'''
s=s[:a]+NEW+s[s.index('- (d) Derivation D1'):]
REP={}
exec(open('rep.py').read())
for k,v in REP.items():
    assert k in s,k
    s=s.replace(k,v)
open('pieces.py','w').write(s)
